,"organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/remitbri/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/remitbri/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/remitbri/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/remitbri/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-02-10T01:37:24Z","updated_at":"2015-02-10T01:37:24Z","body":"Sorry. So:\n.eslintrc\n\n```\n{\n  \"env\" : {\n    \"node\": true,\n  },\n  \"ecmaFeatures\" : {\n    \"jsx\": true\n  },\n  \"rules\" : {\n    \"no-extra-parens\": 2\n  }\n}\n```\n\nmy jsx file\n\n``` jsx\n\"use strict\";\nvar React = require(\"react\");\nvar MyApp = React.createClass({\n  render: function() {\n      return (\n          <div>\n              <h1>{this.props.title}</h1>\n              <form>\n              // and so on\n              </form>\n          </div>\n      );\n  }\n});\nmodule.exports = MyApp;\n```\n\nThe error :\n\n```\n  6:10  error  Gratuitous parentheses around expression  no-extra-parens\n```\n\nI think this is a bug: \n1) parentheses are necessary for this coding style, and this is not a matter of cosmetics like in `(a * b) + c` or `typeof (a)`\n2) the error mentions 6:10, which is where the `<div>` starts, not where the opening parenthesis is (a line before)\n\nIt could be not a bug if it's decided that no, either I write `return <div>` or I switch the no-extra-parens rule off.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/73628511/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"remitbri","id":166973,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Njk3Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/166973?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/remitbri","html_url":"https://github.com/remitbri","followers_url":"https://api.githu